Cosmos board and boot-key support

Source: https://github.com/rianadon/zmk
Revision: 4fc05c26b8faa35081282d58abc84fb6bd1b52bd
License: MIT; see LICENSE-ZMK and individual file headers.

boards/arm/cosmos_lemon_wireless/ is copied unchanged from app/boards/arm/
in that revision. Both the original and v4 hardware definitions are retained.
dts/bindings/zmk,boot-magic-key.yaml is copied from app/dts/bindings/.
The boot-key Kconfig options are copied from app/Kconfig.
src/boot_magic_key.c is based on app/src/boot_magic_key.c, with the bond
clearing implementation from app/src/ble.c. It uses Zephyr sys_reboot and
ZMK v0.3 reset constants instead of the fork-only zmk_reset API. Bootloader
entry, the 500 ms startup window, and optional bond clearing are preserved.
Its SYS_INIT callback uses the Zephyr 3.5 no-argument signature.

The local module allows official ZMK v0.3.0 to build this hardware without
depending on a fork of the entire firmware.
